First of all: Spring Data Neo4j only works with the `@Node` entities for repositories and `Neo4jTemplate` operations. The `@RelationshipProperties` are not meant to be fetched on their own but e.g. via an `Airport` in you case.   
As far as I can see the `Airport` class is also missing a `@Relationship` (or two for both directions) definition completely. For now just assume that you have a definition like

```java
@Relationship(type = &quot;LINE&quot;, direction = Relationship.Direction.INCOMING)
List&lt;Line&gt; incomingFlights;
@Relationship(type = &quot;LINE&quot;, direction = Relationship.Direction.OUTGOING)
List&lt;Line&gt; outgoingFlights;
```

Then you would use an `AirportRepository` to fetch the `Airports` and iterate over their `Lines`.  
If you&#39;re really just interested in the `Lines` w/o any information about start and end node, I would suggest using the `Neo4jClient` which is also part of Spring Data Neo4j but is unaware of the metamodel defined via the annotations.

```java
neo4jClient.query(&quot;&quot;&quot;
	   MATCH (origin:Airport)-[r:LINE]-&gt;(destination:Airport)
	   WHERE id(origin) &lt; id(destination)
	   RETURN r, destination	
		&quot;&quot;&quot;)
		.fetchAs(Line.class)
		.mappedBy((typeSystem, record) -&gt; {
			var lineRelationship = record.get(&quot;r&quot;).asRelationship();
			// populate and return line
		})
		.all();
```

I am explicitly ignoring the `destination` in this example because if you would also be interested in this, you could use a `AirportRepository extends Neo4jRepository&lt;Airport, Long&gt;` and your Java object graph traversal with the returned `Airport` .  
Last but not least, if you want to put this query into an `AirportRepository`, you should not return `r, destination` but `collect(r), destination`. This will create an array to attach to the destination airport for each record. The original query will yield a record for each line/destination combination and thus leave you in the end with just a single `Line` (SDN will overwrite the relationships in the Java collection with the last record)

